      "sequence_position": 17,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(3)$ given below, compute $P(X>5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0498\\,$ | $\\,0.1991\\,$ | $\\,0.4232\\,$ | $\\,0.6472\\,$ | $\\,0.8153\\,$ | $\\,0.9161\\,$ | $\\,0.9665\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>5) & =1-P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =1-F(5) \\\\  & =1-0.9161 \\\\  & =0.0839.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
